# Compositional style

Full write-up: [../boilerplate/docs/composition.md](../../../boilerplate/docs/composition.md) (shared iblokz convention).

Prefer compositional / functional expressions for ordinary prep — not `{ … return … }` when a block is unnecessary.

## Expression bodies & `fn.pipe`

- Prefer `({state, actions}) => header('.top', …)` over `=> { return … }`.
- For a few derived locals, use `fn.pipe` from `iblokz-data` (same spirit as `Promise.then` / Rx `pipe(map, …)`), not an imperative `const` block.

```js
// Prefer
export default ({state, actions}) => fn.pipe(
	() => ({
		open: !!obj.sub(state, ['layout', 'toggles', 'leftSideBar']),
		dim: obj.sub(state, ['layout', 'dim', 'leftSideBar']) || 260
	}),
	({open, dim}) => div('.side-bar', { class: { toggled: open } }, …)
)();

// Avoid
export default ({state, actions}) => {
	const open = !!(state.layout && state.layout.toggles && state.layout.toggles.leftSideBar);
	return div(…);
};
```

Blocks are fine for real control flow / effects — do not force every helper through `fn.pipe`.

## Conditional array composition

Use `[].concat(…, cond ? child : [], …)` — not `null` / `undefined` plus `.filter(Boolean)`.

```js
// Prefer
div('.panel', [].concat(
	header([…]),
	recent.length ? div('.recent', […]) : []
))

// Avoid
div('.panel', [
	header([…]),
	recent.length ? div('.recent', […]) : null
].filter(Boolean))
```
